<http://data.silknow.org/object/ce08638a-3556-3160-b803-5d6681fdbc62>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "One saint wears a pallium over a chasuble, a style of dress that suggests a dating between the eleventh and the twelfth centuries. He is otherwise not vested as an ecclesiastic; the embroidery may therefore have originated outside Europe, possibly at a Coptic community in Egypt. On the other hand, the technique and the architecture, which have something in common with Carolingian art, may suggest a European origin."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/ff6b4ece-4924-3be4-897b-42b66aa22d14> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/bbee4266-819d-3a49-bab6-46c2f56948d9> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/bf817dc8-9fbf-3f4b-86dd-a83613c21e65> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/a6664c78-4d14-3b95-8e18-8aac0763d71d> ;
